# Security

Scope: `implesia-mart-backend` only. The files next to this one are part of the same bar. Follow all of them.

- Public routes do not accept a token and do not reveal whether a hidden record exists.
- Admin routes keep the router role guard. Product writes stay editor or above. User writes stay superadmin. A route guard is not enough; also follow `authorization.mdc`.
- Write models use `extra=forbid`. Do not accept unknown fields.
- Media fields stay on the existing allowlist: one site path, or `https`. Reject `javascript`, `data`, `file`, credentials in the URL, and `..`. Uploaded bytes follow `file-upload.mdc`.
- Escape `LIKE` wildcards. Cap `page` at `10000` and `page_size` at the resource max.
- Public product responses omit `quantity` and `published`. Never return password hashes, tokens, or card data.
- Errors use `{ "error": { "code", "message", "details" } }`. No stack traces.
- Catalog and authenticated responses keep `Cache-Control: no-store`.
- Do not log passwords, tokens, or card data. Do not commit `.env` or secrets.

Also follow: `auth-session.mdc`, `authorization.mdc`, `rate-limiting.mdc`, `http-hardening.mdc`, `database-security.mdc`, `file-upload.mdc`, `commerce-security.mdc`, `audit-logging.mdc`, `secrets-and-dependencies.mdc`.
